## Key Concepts

- A custom model does not mean training a brand-new AI model.
- We can start with an existing model and give it rules for how it should act.
- Ollama uses a model file to set up a custom model.
- The `FROM` section tells Ollama which base model to use.
- Parameters can change how the model responds.
- Temperature controls how random or creative the answers can be.
- The system prompt is one of the most important parts of the model file.
- A system prompt gives the AI instructions that it should follow every time it is used.
- A better base model will usually make the custom model better too.

## What is a Custom Model?

A custom model is a version of an existing AI model that has been set up for a certain job. We are not changing the main model or training it from scratch. Instead, we give it instructions, settings, and examples.

The class example was an email model called Email Guru. The goal was to let the user enter a subject line and have the model create an email without explaining the task every time.

